---
// API & MCP (D190): how a person connects an agent of their own, how-to recipes (Markdown in
// src/api-howto), and a reference of every operation, generated from the same file as the MCP
// server's tools, so it cannot drift from the API.
import { BROWSER_ONLY, MCP_TOOLS } from "@anr/api/mcp-tools";

interface Props {
  /** Where an agent reaches the API: https://api.<root>, or the local API in development. */
  apiBase: string;
}
const { apiBase } = Astro.props;
const mcpUrl = `${apiBase}/mcp`;
const recipes = Object.entries(
  import.meta.glob<{ frontmatter: { title: string; who: string }; Content: unknown }>(
    "../../api-howto/*.md",
    { eager: true },
  ),
)
  .sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b))
  .map(([file, module]) => ({ id: file.replace(/^.*\/\d+-|\.md$/g, ""), ...module }));
const WHO = {
  anyone: "anyone signed in",
  member: "any member",
  "editor-in-chief": "Editor-in-Chief",
  "platform-admin": "platform admin",
} as const;
const claudeCode = `claude mcp add --transport http anr ${mcpUrl} \\
  --header "Authorization: Bearer $ANR_TOKEN"`;
const json = JSON.stringify(
  { mcpServers: { anr: { type: "http", url: mcpUrl, headers: { Authorization: "Bearer anr_…" } } } },
  null,
  2,
);
const env = `export ANR_API=${apiBase}
export ANR_TOKEN=anr_…   # from the Tokens page`;
---
<h1>API &amp; MCP</h1>
<p>
  Everything you can do on this desk, an agent of your own can do through ANR's API or its MCP
  server: Claude Code, an assistant app, a script. It acts as you, with your roles and nothing more,
  and what it does is yours. An approval it makes is your approval, and the audit log names the
  token it came through.
</p>
<nav class="toc">
  <a href="#start">Get started</a> · <a href="#mcp">Connect an MCP client</a> ·
  <a href="#http">Call the HTTP API</a> · <a href="#howto">How-tos</a> ·
  <a href="#reference">Reference</a>
</nav>

<h2 id="start">Get started</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Issue a personal token on the <a href="/me/tokens">Tokens</a> page. It is shown once. It expires after 90 days unless you choose otherwise, and you can revoke it there at any time.</li>
  <li>Give it only to an agent you control. Anyone holding it can do whatever you can.</li>
  <li>Connect the agent to the MCP server, or call the HTTP API with it.</li>
</ol>
<p class="meta">
  Tokens are issued and revoked only here on the desk, never with a token. ANR's own newsroom
  agents (the planner, the desk, the fact-checker and the rest) never get this server, and never
  add it to LM Studio's MCP servers for them: they keep their four tools.
</p>

<h2 id="mcp">Connect an MCP client</h2>
<p>The server is at <code>{mcpUrl}</code> (Streamable HTTP). It has one tool per API operation, named by its operation id.</p>
<h3>Claude Code</h3>
<pre><code>{claudeCode}</code></pre>
<h3>Other clients (JSON configuration)</h3>
<pre><code>{json}</code></pre>
<p>Ask the agent to start with <code>getDeskMe</code>: it returns your newsrooms by slug and your role in each, and most tools take that slug as <code>newsroom</code>.</p>

<h2 id="http">Call the HTTP API</h2>
<pre><code>{env}</code></pre>
<pre><code>curl -s "$ANR_API/desk/me" -H "Authorization: Bearer $ANR_TOKEN"</code></pre>
<p>
  The contract is <a href={`${apiBase}/openapi.yaml`}><code>{apiBase}/openapi.yaml</code></a> (OpenAPI 3.1).
  Errors are JSON, <code>{"{"}"error": "…"{"}"}</code>:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>401</strong>: no token, or it was revoked or has expired.</li>
  <li><strong>403</strong>: your role cannot do this, or it can only be done here on the desk.</li>
  <li><strong>404</strong>: nothing with that id in this newsroom.</li>
  <li><strong>409</strong>: the thing is not in a state that allows it, such as a publication changed since you read it.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="howto">How-tos</h2>
<p>Each step names the MCP tool; the HTTP call is the same operation.</p>
{recipes.map((r) => {
  const Content = r.Content as any;
  return (
    <details class="card" id={r.id}>
      <summary><strong>{r.frontmatter.title}</strong> <span class="meta">· {r.frontmatter.who}</span></summary>
      <Content />
    </details>
  );
})}

<h2 id="reference">Reference</h2>
<p>{MCP_TOOLS.length} tools, one per operation a token may call.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table class="reference">
  <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>HTTP</th><th>Who</th><th>Kind</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{MCP_TOOLS.map((t) => (
    <tr>
      <td><code>{t.name}</code><br /><small>{t.title}</small></td>
      <td><code>{t.method} {t.path}</code></td>
      <td>{WHO[t.who]}</td>
      <td>{t.readOnly ? "reads" : t.destructive ? "decides or stops" : "changes"}</td>
    </tr>
  ))}</tbody>
</table></div>
<h3>Only on the desk</h3>
<ul>{BROWSER_ONLY.map((o) => <li><code>{o.method} {o.path}</code>: {o.title}</li>)}</ul>

<style>
  pre, details :global(pre.astro-code) {
    overflow-x: auto; background: #f5f5f4 !important; color: #1c1917 !important;
    padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 6px;
  }
  details :global(pre.astro-code span) { color: inherit !important; }
  .toc { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  table.reference td { vertical-align: top; }
  details.card summary { cursor: pointer; min-height: 44px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
